Q3532158 | power, trade | south | Venad, also known as Quilon, was a medieval state between the Western Ghats and the Arabian Sea at the south-western tip of India. | Venad was a small kingdom at the very southern tip of India, between the mountains and the sea.
Q3536222 | arts, religion | south | The Chennakeshava Temple at Belur, in the Hassan district of Karnataka, is a 12th-century Hindu temple. | The Chennakeshava Temple at Belur is covered in fine stone carvings. It is about 900 years old.
