Q1720882 | power | west | Cutch State was a kingdom in the Kutch region from 1147 to 1819, and afterwards a princely state. | Kutch, in the far west of India, was its own kingdom for almost 700 years.
Q3634368 | power, daily, technology | north | Jaisalmer Fort in Rajasthan is one of the very few "living forts" in the world: a large part of the old city's people still live inside it. | People still live inside the walls of Jaisalmer Fort, in the desert of Rajasthan.
Q1678784 | power | north | The Kingdom of Jaisalmer, in the far west of today's Rajasthan, lasted from the mid-12th century until 1947. It dates from 1156, the time of Rawal Jaisal. | The desert kingdom of Jaisalmer began in 1156 and lasted almost 800 years.
Q3517561 | arts, religion | south | The Hoysaleswara temple at Halebidu is a 12th-century Hindu temple dedicated to Shiva, and the largest monument there. | The Hoysaleswara temple at Halebidu has walls covered with thousands of carvings.
